  "member_id": "el-manira-abdel",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B007",
        "laureates": [
          "Jacques F. A. P. Miller",
          "Max D. Cooper"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of distinct B- and T-lymphocyte lineages and their roles in adaptive immunity"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B016",
    "B014"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B007 identifies a precise, durable biological discovery: adaptive immunity comprises distinct lymphocyte lineages with complementary roles. This framework has exceptional explanatory reach across immunology and medicine, while Miller and Cooper provide a compact and complementary attribution for the linked T- and B-lineage discoveries. The citation deliberately recognizes that defined advance rather than the wider development of modern immunology.",
    "case_against": "The historical work spans different experimental systems and additional contributors. Even a narrowly framed two-person award therefore requires care not to imply that Miller and Cooper alone account for all subsequent understanding of adaptive immunity. B016 and B014 remain especially serious alternatives because each combines mature evidence with a more readily delimited technical achievement.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius argues that HPV virus-like-particle vaccines couple a bounded scientific advance to mature, large-scale prevention of infection and related cancers, with Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller forming a coherent trio.",
        "response": "I agree that B016 has extraordinary preventive significance and is the strongest alternative to B007. The remaining question is whether the proposed trio can be separated sufficiently from the broader virology, vaccine-development, and implementation pathway. I retain B007 first because its central biological conclusion and paired attribution are more settled, while recognizing that prevention of HPV-associated cancer is an exceptional medical achievement."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson places chaperonin-assisted protein folding first because it is a mature, experimentally grounded mechanism with a focused Horwich-Hartl attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that B014 is an unusually cleanly bounded fundamental discovery and that its citation can distinguish chaperonin action from the wider folding field. I nevertheless retain B007 because defining the distinct lymphocyte systems supplied an organizing biological architecture whose consequences extend directly through immune function, disease mechanisms, and clinical practice. Both are mature foundational achievements; B007 has the stronger comparative medical and explanatory reach."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "sandberg-rickard",
        "point": "Sandberg prioritizes antisense correction of SMN2 splicing because a defined molecular mechanism produced transformative treatment for spinal muscular atrophy.",
        "response": "B021 compellingly demonstrates mechanism-based therapeutic benefit. Its proposed pair nonetheless sits within a distributed chain involving SMA genetics, antisense chemistry, clinical trials, and delivery. That attribution boundary is more difficult than B007's bounded recognition of complementary lineage discoveries, so I do not change my ordering."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the historical record can be represented narrowly enough to credit Miller and Cooper fully for the linked lineage discoveries without minimizing other essential contributors.",
      "Whether the Committee should ultimately give greater comparative weight to B016's direct population-level prevention of HPV-associated cancers than to B007's foundational explanatory reach."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No connection to the proposed laureates or achievement is apparent from the supplied profile. The profile records a 2009 co-authored paper with committee member Thomas Perlmann; it does not concern B007 or its proposed laureates."
  }
}
